From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The weather's drops all over the wider, taller screen (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A weather's sprites (the rain's drops, the snow's flakes, the sand) live
on the DS's screen with 64 pixels round it: they come on there, go off
one side and on at the other (ov5_021D630C), and the weather's sprite
surface shows only those on the DS's 256 x 192. On the 3DS's wider upper
screen, and the field at the DS's pixel size (400 x 240), the weather
showed in the DS's part of it alone.

Now, with the screen wider or taller (NitroPort_EngineABeside: ex
columns each side, et lines above and below; 0 and 0 on the DS's, all as
before):
- the weather's surface shows its cells on the whole picture
  (RenderOam_PortInitSurfaceBeside);
- the drops go round the wider screen with 64 pixels round it
  (ov5_PortPlaceWide);
- each comes on where the game puts it on the DS's screen, stretched
  onto the wider one, or as far beside the wider one as the game has it
  beside the DS's (its first place after ov5_021D6F00, where the DS has
  it going round);
- more of them come on for the wider screen's area, width or height, as
  each weather brings them on all over it, along its top or down its
  side (ov5_PortWeatherCount; the pool of 48 as before), and the ones a
  weather brings on at once as it starts are moved on as far as their
  place among them has it (ov5_021D7568);
- they're taken away as far below or above the wider screen as the
  game has them below or above the DS's (the snow's, the ash's, the
  spirits').

